Gram matrix G_I =
⎡ 1   1/2  1/2   0 ⎤
⎢                  ⎥
⎢1/2   1    0   1/2⎥
⎢                  ⎥
⎢1/2   0    1   1/2⎥
⎢                  ⎥
⎣ 0   1/2  1/2   1 ⎦
det(G_I) = 0

======================================================================
THE QUADRUPLE IS LINEARLY DEPENDENT
======================================================================
    The Gram matrix of the four chosen facet normals is singular,
    so this quadruple determines no vertex by Cramer's rule: the
    four hyperplanes meet in a line rather than a point, or not at
    all.  That degeneracy is what this diagnostic was written to
    detect, and it is why the vertex solvers elsewhere in the
    package try every independent subset of the active facets
    rather than taking the first four (see
    arc1_v1w1/region4_exact_volume.py).
